; expect 80
; A range-constrained subtype conversion that does not hold, and the
; status a failed check exits with.
;
; 80 IS THE CONTRACT TRAP, and sharing it is the point of the case.
; A subtype adds no new enforcement mechanism over a `pre`
; (`docs/subtypes-design.md` Question 1): the conversion is a
; compare, a branch, and a call to `@__axiom_contract_fail`, which
; `docs/memory-model.md` MM-EXEC-16 reserves status 80 for since
; 2026-09-08 (roadmap item 11, D3). A supervisor reading a status
; therefore tells a range violation from an out-of-range index (77)
; the same way it tells a violated contract from one.
;
; The check exercised here is the CALL-ARGUMENT one: `takePos`
; declares `(-> Positive Int)` and 99 is outside `1 .. 10`, so the
; call traps before the body runs. The cast half takes the same path
; through the same trap and would pin the same number twice.
;
; The message and the backtrace go to fd 2 and are not this gate's
; subject - `scripts/check-contracts.sh` reads that shape.
(subtype Positive is Int range 1 .. 10)

(:: takePos (-> Positive Int))

(fn (takePos x) x)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (takePos 99))
